  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "k >= B(A) = log P / max_p e_p log p, and B(A) is exactly the strength of the product route.",
      "id": "T1",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "claim": "H_{p,t} is a disjoint union of complete bipartite graphs on antipodal class pairs plus cliques on self-antipodal classes.",
      "id": "T2",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "claim": "N_t(p) <= min(C(n,2), (n/2)(X/p^t + 1)).",
      "id": "T3",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Ceiling. Counting+range+residue estimates give at most k >= 1+o(1); adding gcd normalisation and one-step recursion, at most k >= 2+o(1). The product route cannot reproduce Erdos-Turan's log_2 n.",
      "id": "T4",
      "status": "proved",
      "witness_families": [
        "Omega'(n,p,m) = {1} u {i p^m}",
        "Omega(n,p,m) = {i p^m + 1} u {j p^m - 1}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "For every prime q outside S, A occupies at most (q+1)/2 classes mod q; |A| <= 2 whenever 2 is not in S.",
      "id": "P5a",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "claim": "n <= 3(X+Q^2)/(pi(Q)-k); in particular n = O(sqrt(X) log X).",
      "id": "P5b",
      "status": "derived-not-independently-checked"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Smooth-counting lane is capped: k >= log n / loglog(2X), which beats log_2 n only if X < e^2. Capped below Erdos-Turan even granting X <= n^C.",
      "id": "P5d",
      "status": "proved"
    },
    {
      "claim": "r_186989 loose thread 3 ('prove |A| <= p-1 by pigeonhole mod p') is false as stated; {1+iM} with M a product of odd primes is antipodal-free mod every odd q <= Q at any size. Replacement is P5a.",
      "id": "A1",
      "status": "audit"
    },
    {
      "claim": "r_186989 sections 2 and 4 proofs check out; its seven witnesses re-verified valid by independent trial division. Exhaustiveness of its searches not re-run.",
      "id": "A2",
      "status": "audit"
    }
  ],
  "note": "Erdos #126 analytic arm. Not evidence for or against RH.",
